{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-09_12-07-35-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('map.json'))\np['version']=13\nco=p['core_overview']\nco['open_details']=[\n \\\"appendEntries has an explicit TODO (raft.go:1541): if StoreLogs fails after a truncation, lastLog is left stale. Whether any real store can fail there, and its consequence, is unresolved.\\\",\n \\\"electSelf returns a nil response channel when persisting the self-vote fails (raft.go:2023), leaving the candidate to wait out its election timer; this is a storage-failure path only.\\\",\n \\\"checkLeaderLease assumes leaderState.replState contains every voter of the latest configuration (raft.go:1054); ordering on the main thread appears to guarantee this, but a nil-map lookup would panic and was not tested.\\\",\n \\\"The pre-vote path treats a transport 'unexpected command' error as a granted pre-vote (raft.go:2084-2090), which is intentional for mixed versions but was not analysed for a genuinely unreachable peer.\\\",\n \\\"Four implementation-level duties on the mapped paths are confirmed in scope and belong to their claim/check records rather than here: batching FSMs never receive ConfigurationStore.StoreConfiguration (claim-config-store-delivery); the heartbeat fast path reaches appendEntries without checkRPCHeader (claim-heartbeat-header-gate); TimeoutNow grants the pre-vote-skipping vote privilege without attributing the sender to the configuration (claim-timeout-now-attribution); and an accepted InstallSnapshot retains and reports an unconfirmed log tail (claim-install-snapshot-alignment). Their residual premises - real-deployment reachability, election/quorum consequence, contract exemption and tail lifetime - remain open.\\\",\n \\\"The ReloadConfig notification scope (only a decreased HeartbeatTimeout signals the notify channels) and the processHeartbeat concurrency contract are recorded as leads/limits with no obligation.\\\"\n]\nopen('map.json','w').write(json.dumps(p,indent=1))\nprint('version',p['version'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-09_12-07-35-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('map.json'))\np['version']=13\nco=p['core_overview']\nco['open_details']=[\n \\\"appendEntries has an explicit TODO (raft.go:1541): if StoreLogs fails after a truncation, lastLog is left stale. Whether any real store can fail there, and its consequence, is unresolved.\\\",\n \\\"electSelf returns a nil response channel when persisting the self-vote fails (raft.go:2023), leaving the candidate to wait out its election timer; this is a storage-failure path only.\\\",\n \\\"checkLeaderLease assumes leaderState.replState contains every voter of the latest configuration (raft.go:1054); ordering on the main thread appears to guarantee this, but a nil-map lookup would panic and was not tested.\\\",\n \\\"The pre-vote path treats a transport 'unexpected command' error as a granted pre-vote (raft.go:2084-2090), which is intentional for mixed versions but was not analysed for a genuinely unreachable peer.\\\",\n \\\"Four implementation-level duties on the mapped paths are confirmed in scope and belong to their claim/check records rather than here: batching FSMs never receive ConfigurationStore.StoreConfiguration (claim-config-store-delivery); the heartbeat fast path reaches appendEntries without checkRPCHeader (claim-heartbeat-header-gate); TimeoutNow grants the pre-vote-skipping vote privilege without attributing the sender to the configuration (claim-timeout-now-attribution); and an accepted InstallSnapshot retains and reports an unconfirmed log tail (claim-install-snapshot-alignment). Their residual premises - real-deployment reachability, election/quorum consequence, contract exemption and tail lifetime - remain open.\\\",\n \\\"The ReloadConfig notification scope (only a decreased HeartbeatTimeout signals the notify channels) and