{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"submission_c26.json\",\"summary\":\"Small consolidation product: the core overview now navigates to the run's confirmed results instead of leaving them only in claim records; preflight-validated with valid=True and no diagnostics.\\n\\nWhat changed: core_overview.open_details keeps the four original local anomalies and gains two navigation entries — one naming the four confirmed in-scope duties on the mapped paths (batching FSMs never receive ConfigurationStore.StoreConfiguration; the heartbeat fast path reaches appendEntries without checkRPCHeader while the normal path rejects the same request; TimeoutNow grants the pre-vote-skipping vote privilege to a sender the receiver's configuration does not contain; an accepted InstallSnapshot retains and reports a log tail above the snapshot index) with their residual premises, and one naming the ReloadConfig notification-scope lead and the processHeartbeat concurrency limit. Formation, context, connection, status and core_gaps are untouched, so form stays navigation and the claims/checks/assessments keep ownership of the reasoning and evidence.\\n\\nThe feedback also records three suspicions that were excluded rather than escalated: the protocol-version gate cannot underflow (ProtocolVersion is a signed int, so the window the fast path skips is real); liveBootstrap cannot bootstrap a node with existing state (BootstrapCluster refuses on HasExistingState); and FileSnapshotStore.List does not alias its metadata in this toolchain (a local run listed three snapshots with distinct, correctly ordered metadata, recorded as construction knowledge with the toolchain caveat).\\n\\nStill open: the residual premises of the four confirmed findings (real reachability of an unconfigured TimeoutNow sender, election/quorum consequence of the fast-path heartbeat, whether batching FSMs are contractually exempt from ConfigurationStore, and the lifetime of a snapshot-installed tail under a live leader), the ReloadConfig and processHeartbeat leads, and the still-unread in-memory snapshot store, observer plumbing, and net_transport beyond the classification and pipeline review.\"}"}}
